  Accuracy            0.6940    0.9266    0.1392    0.4360    0.9965    1.0000    1.0000   5.0%  0.9524   -1.67
  Logit Diff          1.2461    2.3139    0.9683   -0.0431    2.4871    3.7095    4.0350  15.0%  0.8571   -1.10
  KL Div              0.1902    0.0717    0.1118    0.0021    0.0279    0.2046    0.4936   5.0%  0.9524   -1.06
  Exact Match         0.7060    0.9315    0.1317    0.4620    0.9965    1.0000    1.0000   5.0%  0.9524   -1.71
  -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  pct = the discovered circuit's percentile in the null (direction-aware);
  p = Monte-Carlo p-value (#random at least as good + 1) / (n + 1);
  z = (discovered - mean) / std, signed so positive is better.

  READ EVERY COLUMN BACKWARDS HERE. `pct` and `z` follow Task.metric_better,
  which is written for a circuit that should REPRODUCE the full model. This
  knockout is meant to BREAK it, so on all four metrics the necessity result is
  a LOW percentile:
    accuracy, logit diff   low pct = less deceptive behaviour survives the
                           circuit's knockout than a random one's
    KL div, exact match    low pct = the circuit's knockout moved the prediction
                           further from the full model's than a random one did
  A high percentile on any of them says a random circuit of this size would have
  done the job as well, or better.

